I added the last missing piece of #1054 and committed it as 40c2b68e. The commit title says Fixes #1054, so the issue will close when this is pushed. Build, clippy and fmt pass, and all 7034 tests pass, including the version-claim test and the module-size test.

What changed:
• `src/tool_wrappers.rs`: two places put a note in front of the answer: the "this sub-agent result is PARTIAL" note in annotate_if_partial, and the "switched to the fallback model" note. Each now has a comment saying the model sees the answer along with the note only since yoagent 0.25.9. Before that, the model saw only the note and not the answer. Each comment ends with a // yoagent-version-claim: 0.25 line. The fallback comment used to say "as its own block", which is the wording found wrong on Day 239. It now says that on the Anthropic wire the text blocks are joined with "\n" into one string. I checked that against yoagent 0.25.16's provider::tool_result_text.
• `src/smart_edit.rs`: the same comment and marker on both notes it adds. One correction to the plan: it called both "elevated-risk note pushes", but the second one (~l.565) is actually the whitespace auto-fix note, so its comment says that.
• `ARCHITECTURE.md`: one sentence each on the smart_edit.rs and tool_wrappers.rs entries, with <!-- yoagent-version-claim: 0.25 -->.
• `tests/module_size.rs`: tool_wrappers.rs was already exactly at its size limit (5724 lines), so the 8 comment lines meant raising its entry to 5732. The reason is written in the entry.

Checks for anything left over:
• Images: when a result includes an image, yoagent sends the full block array instead of joining the text. Every block is still sent, so none of these notes can get lost that way. I filed no follow-up issue.
• Request-level tests: only the hook site has one (tests/hook_feedback_request.rs), and the other four don't. That test still covers them: all five sites go through the same yoagent join, so it fails if that join ever drops a non-first block again. If a wrapper stopped adding its note at all, the existing per-site unit tests would catch it. This reasoning is in the commit body.
• References to #1054: git grep '#1054' src docs skills finds one hit, a past-tense history note in src/hooks.rs:1374 ("built and dropped (#1054)"). It stays accurate after the issue closes, so I left it.
